<div class="container">
    <h2>About AnimoSync</h2>
    <p class="warning-text">
        Below is a comprehensive list of the NPM packages and third-party libraries utilized in the development of AnimoSync.
    </p>

    <div class="profile-card">
        <h3>NPM Packages (Backend Dependencies)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>express:</strong> The core web application framework for Node.js used to handle routing and server logic.</li>
            <li><strong>express-handlebars:</strong> The template engine used to render dynamic HTML views.</li>
            <li><strong>mongoose:</strong> An Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for MongoDB and Node.js used to manage database connections and schemas.</li>
            <li><strong>express-session:</strong> Middleware used to manage and store user session data for secure authentication.</li>
        </ul>

        <br>

        <h3>Third-Party Libraries (Frontend)</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>jQuery:</strong> A fast, small, and feature-rich JavaScript library used for easier DOM manipulation and event handling across the frontend.</li>
            <li><strong>Fetch API:</strong> (Native JS) Used for making asynchronous HTTP requests to our backend API endpoints.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <br>
        
        <h3>Core Technologies</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Node.js:</strong> JavaScript runtime environment executing the backend code.</li>
            <li><strong>MongoDB:</strong> NoSQL database used for storing users, admins, labs, and reservations.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>